<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1.0/policyconfig.dtd">
<policyconfig>
  <!--
    Potluck mesh sidecar — Linux polkit action.

    NOTE ON THIS COMMENT'S PLACEMENT AND WORDING: XML forbids the two-hyphen
    sequence anywhere inside a comment body (only legal as the closing
    marker) — libxml2/glib's parser, which polkitd uses, rejects the WHOLE
    FILE on that violation, and polkitd 0.105 (Ubuntu 22.04's version) does
    this silently: `pkaction` just reports "No action with action id ..."
    with nothing explaining why in the polkit journal (confirmed
    empirically while building this file — a CLI-flag example originally
    written here with real double-hyphen flags broke registration). So:
    no double hyphens anywhere below, and this comment sits AFTER
    <policyconfig>, not between the DOCTYPE and the root element, purely
    for readability (that placement was NOT itself the bug).

    Installed to /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/ai.trypotluck.mesh.policy by
    the .deb/.rpm postinst (or, in dev, by hand — see
    packaging/linux/README.md).

    This binds ONE fixed action id to ONE fixed, root-owned, non-writable
    script path via org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path. That annotation is
    what gives us a friendly branded prompt ("Install and start Potluck
    mesh networking") instead of pkexec's generic "Authenticate to run
    /path/to/script" message — see mesh-install-helper.sh's header comment
    for why the path itself, not this policy file, is the actual security
    boundary: pkexec independently refuses to run anything that isn't
    root-owned and non-group/other-writable, regardless of what this file
    says. This file only controls the PROMPT and the AUTHORIZATION RULE
    (who gets asked, and what "yes" requires); it does not and cannot
    expand what the target script is allowed to do.

    main.js's mesh:enable IPC handler on Linux invokes pkexec against this
    exact helper path with a fixed "install" subcommand and a fixed set of
    flags (coordinator url, derp url, mesh binary path, uid, gid) — see
    mesh-install-helper.sh's own header comment for the literal argument
    list, since it can't be spelled out here without hyphens. main.js NEVER
    constructs this action id or policy content itself, and
    the renderer never sees or influences the pkexec invocation directly
    (it only calls the whitelisted mesh:enable IPC channel with no
    arguments of its own — see main.js's ipcMain.handle('mesh:enable', ...)
    for the fixed argument list actually passed).

    auth_admin (not auth_admin_keep): every install/uninstall re-prompts.
    This is a rare, one-time-per-machine action (or an explicit
    user-initiated uninstall) — we deliberately do NOT cache admin auth
    across calls the way a frequently-used action might, since that would
    leave a wider window where ANY process could pkexec this script
    without a fresh password.
  -->
  <vendor>Potluck AI</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://trypotluck.ai</vendor_url>

  <action id="ai.trypotluck.mesh.install">
    <description>Install and manage the Potluck mesh networking service</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to install Potluck's mesh networking service</message>
    <icon_name>ai.trypotluck.app</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>auth_admin</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>auth_admin</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/lib/potluck/mesh-install-helper.sh</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
